# Server-side appointment automation (Cloudflare Worker secrets; never NEXT_PUBLIC_*).
# Deploy the scheduled runner with: npm run appointments:deploy
# Configure GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID and GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET, then add separate
# refresh tokens: GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN with calendar.events scope and
# GOOGLE_MAIL_REFRESH_TOKEN with gmail.send scope authorized as
# turnaroundexpertshp@gmail.com. Also configure FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL and
# FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY for the notifier Worker. Add each value as an encrypted
# Cloudflare secret for turnaroundexperts-appointment-notifier; do not paste
# secret values into Git or chat. Missing secrets leave notification jobs queued.
# From the repository root, run each command and enter its value at the prompt:
# npx wrangler secret put FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL --config wrangler.appointments.jsonc
# npx wrangler secret put FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY --config wrangler.appointments.jsonc
# npx wrangler secret put GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID --config wrangler.appointments.jsonc
# npx wrangler secret put GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET --config wrangler.appointments.jsonc
# npx wrangler secret put GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN --config wrangler.appointments.jsonc
# npx wrangler secret put GOOGLE_MAIL_REFRESH_TOKEN --config wrangler.appointments.jsonc
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN=
GOOGLE_MAIL_REFRESH_TOKEN=
# Optional; defaults to the primary calendar of the OAuth account.
GOOGLE_CALENDAR_ID=primary
# Mail is sent through Gmail API as turnaroundexpertshp@gmail.com.
APP_BASE_URL=https://turnaroundexperts.in
